{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:a22d742a030acd83","name":"AT-RCT","source":{"id":"source:reference-a22d742a030acd83","title":"AT-RCT","revision":15633,"timestamp":"2024-08-18T00:52:57Z","sha256":"802c9021077feebf3bea9a7069dcf181693cae6547dddb2e161f7d6287565250","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=15633","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=AT-RCT&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-a22d742a030acd83","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Legacy Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Legacy_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Fel Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Fel_Empire","referenceId":"reference:45bef1c82bffe9c1"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The urban successor to the ",{"tag":"a","children":["AT-ST"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/AT-ST","referenceId":"reference:42d3fc5263e8fdb5"},", the All Terrain Riot Control Transport is designed for use in cities and other highly developed areas with large populations. Based on designs dating back to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"},", the AT-RCT features an open cockpit, allowing the crew full 360-degree vision and the ability to fire personal weapons at targets approaching from lines of fire outside of the AT-RCT's own fire arcs. Unfortunately, this also leaves the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Copilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Copilot","referenceId":"reference:49f5b0e488cfa66c"}," open to attacks from the ground, though the AT-RCT's primary mission is crowd control and riot suppression, which usually means dealing with unruly (though not usually well-armed) mobs. Additionally, since the AT-RCT is used in support of ground troops, there is usually enough suppressing fire in the area to protect the crew.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The AT-RCT operates effectively in urban sprawls where the terrain is hindered by narrow alleys, winding streets, and uneven surfaces. With a more narrow front profile than the ",{"tag":"a","children":["AT-ST"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/AT-ST","referenceId":"reference:42d3fc5263e8fdb5"},", the AT-RCT can usually turn 180 degrees in a single spot, allowing it to get in and out of tight places where ",{"tag":"a","children":["Speeders"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Speeders","referenceId":"reference:be93ac2e4867f0ca"}," are impractical. Thanks to the insurgency of both ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Alliance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Alliance","referenceId":"reference:bd53073ee6d4d9a0"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Fel Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Fel_Empire","referenceId":"reference:45bef1c82bffe9c1"},", the AT-RCT has seen greatly increased use on Imperial worlds throughout the galaxy.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Expert)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["AT-RCT Statistics (CL 8)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Huge ",{"tag":"a","children":["Walker"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Walker"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +10; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +8\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","childr